  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Shelter and NFI assistance to communities affected by floods in 2022</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this $2.5 million UNHCR project is to address the immediate shelter and non-food item needs of some of the most severely flood-affected people. To that end, UNHCR will provide $1.8 million in cash assistance to support the shelter needs of 30,000 people. Additionally, UNHCR will distribute essential household items to 20,000 cash recipients to respond to additional needs, among other activities. In total, UNHCR will reach 30,000 people, including 6,874 women, 9,651 girls and 4,500 persons living with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
